Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David Moreno <dmoreno@coralbits.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/davidmoreno/aseqrc/
X-Build-Distro: @DISTRO@
X-Build-Id: @BUILD_ID@
Description: Control ALSA Sequencer connections via web
 aseqrc runs a small HTTP server that controls the connections of the ALSA
 sequencer, so a machine with all the MIDI gear attached (a Raspberry Pi with
 no monitor, for example) can be patched from a phone or a tablet.
 .
 The web interface is a PWA: it can be installed as an app from the browser.
 .
 The dependency list is generated by dpkg-shlibdeps inside the container of the
 distribution this package was built on, so it matches that release exactly.
